// A reactive `for` that cascades (Inputs/tree_reactive.ent): a node is
// placed where its own Local changed or the World above it did, which the
// same `for` may just have done, so a change goes down the tree in the
// pass that sees it and nothing else is visited. As the tree is, the
// `for` goes from the events down the children's links (the lowered
// program counts the zeros below a mark). Sorted, the tree is in two
// archetypes here (the root has no Local) and the `for` goes through
// every row; with a Local for the root it is in one, and the `for` goes
// from the events down the rows' child ranges. All give the same lines,
// the sorted ones in another order of rows.
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent -I %S/../../devices %S/Inputs/tree_reactive.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | ent-opt --ent-lower-to-loops 2>/dev/null | grep -q "llvm.intr.cttz"
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/tree_reactive.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.out
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/tree_reactive.ent 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.out
// RUN: sed 's/ tree capacity 16/ tree sorted capacity 16/' \
// RUN:     %S/Inputs/tree_reactive.ent > %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: grep -q "tree sorted" %t.sorted.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.sorted.ent 2>/dev/null | sort > %t.sorted.out
// RUN: sort %t.out | cmp - %t.sorted.out
// RUN: sed -e 's/placed: 0 } }/placed: 0 }, Local { x: 0 } }/' \
// RUN:     -e 's/World without Local where Frame == 5/World, l: Local where Frame == 5 \&\& l.x == 0/' \
// RUN:     %t.sorted.ent > %t.one.ent
// RUN: grep -q "l.x == 0" %t.one.ent
// RUN: grep -q "Local { x: 0 }" %t.one.ent
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent -I %S/../../devices %t.one.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | ent-opt --ent-lower-to-loops 2>/dev/null | grep -q "llvm.intr.cttz"
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent -I %S/../../devices %t.sorted.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | ent-opt --ent-lower-to-loops 2>/dev/null | not grep -q "llvm.intr.cttz"
// RUN: %ent run %t.one.ent 2>/dev/null | sort | cmp - %t.sorted.out
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// root <- a <- a1 <- a11, a <- a2, root <- b <- b1.
// CHECK:      1: root 1 placed 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a 11 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b 21 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a1 111 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a2 211 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: b1 321 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: a11 1111 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 6 placed
// What the pass wrote the frame before is no news to it.
// CHECK:      2: a11 1111 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: 0 placed
// a moves: a, and a1, a2 and a11 below it.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root 1 placed 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a 12 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b 21 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a1 112 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a2 212 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: b1 321 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: a11 1112 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: 4 placed
// A leaf: itself alone.
// CHECK:      4: b1 322 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: a11 1112 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: 1 placed
// The root, changed by another system: everything below it.
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: root 2 placed 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: a 13 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: b 22 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: a1 113 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: a2 213 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: b1 323 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: a11 1113 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 5: 6 placed
// CHECK:      6: 0 placed
// A node made and connected under a: itself alone.
// CHECK:      7: a3 413 placed 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 7: 1 placed
// a moves again, with the new node below it.
// CHECK:      8: a 14 placed 4
// CHECK:      8: b1 323 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 8: a11 1114 placed 4
// CHECK-NEXT: 8: a3 414 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 8: 5 placed
// a1 is put under b: it and a11 below it are placed from there, though
// nothing of theirs or of b's has changed.
// CHECK:      9: b 22 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: a1 122 placed 5
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: a2 214 placed 4
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: b1 323 placed 3
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: a11 1122 placed 5
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: a3 414 placed 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 9: 2 placed
// CHECK:      10: 0 placed
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
